<spell-notebook "checkbox theming">
	<header level="1">
		Checkbox
		<header>A checkbox allows a user to select a value from a small set of options, often binary.</>
	</>
	<checkbox-tab-bar showing="theming"/>
	<section>
		<menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
			<item link="#tokens">Tokens</>
			<item link="#themes">Themes</>
		</>
	</>

	<!-- THEMING:  the family's tokens, live, plus how to set them and which themes touch it. -->
	<section label="Tokens">
		<markdown>
			Theme with the public `--ui-checkbox-*` tokens: set one on the element, on any ancestor (a form, `:root`), or on
			the root box through `::part(checkbox)`. They inherit into the shadow root, where the sheet reads each through a
			private alias, so nothing inside blocks them; radios, sliders and toggles read the same set. Style the other
			pieces with `::part()`: `control` and `label`.
		</>
		<markdown>
			```css
			ui-checkbox,
			ui-radio {
			  --ui-checkbox-toggle-lane-on: var(--ui-positive);
			  --ui-checkbox-radius: 0;
			}
			```
		</>
		<message state="info" size="small">
			<markdown>
				`inverted` swaps in its own `--ui-checkbox-inverted-*` colours, and `color` re-points the chosen colours at the
				hue. Never set the `--_ui-checkbox-*` names: they're the sheet's private plumbing.
			</>
		</>
		<markdown>Edit a value below to try it.</>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-tokens family="ui-checkbox" playground>
				<ui-checkbox>Make my profile visible</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Themes">
		<markdown>
			The theme menu above picks the theme for every page of the site:  Spell, Glass, Fruity or Merlot,
			each restyling this component through its tokens.
		</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
